+# gigi/3-forensics: gemma-3 has no tool-call tokens. Through OpenRouter (DeepInfra) it writes its
+# call as text in its own format, e.g. ```tool_code\n[execute_command(command='ls')]\n```, which
+# the harness reads as a prose reply (ending the run, or nudging it into a loop of apologies).
+# When a reply has no structured tool call, the first call in such a block that names one of the
+# offered tools becomes a structured call (a block counts only if it calls a tool by name). The
+# text stays in the message unchanged. An empty reply (no text, no call) is a provider glitch, not
+# a choice: it is retried like a missing one instead of being read as the agent's final reply.
